<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV7N45/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV7N45/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV7N45/>;
    dc:modified '2007-11-21T17:19:40'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'beaufort_wind_force'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Beaufort wind force" is an index assigned on the Beaufort wind force scale and relates a qualitative description of the degree of disturbance or destruction caused by wind to the speed of the wind. The Beaufort wind scale varies between 0 (qualitatively described as calm, smoke rises vertically, sea appears glassy) (wind speeds in the range 0 - 0.2 m s-1) and 12 (hurricane, wave heights in excess of 14 m) (wind speeds in excess of 32.7 m s-1).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV7N45'^^xsd:string .
